{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:BraidsAndKnots.BarInvolution","@type":"LeanModule","name":"BraidsAndKnots.BarInvolution","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":44,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.bar_half","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.bar_half","kind":"theorem","line":380,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/bar-involution.lean#L380-L382","doc":"`bar(1/2) = 1/2` — the field-division form of `bar_invOf_two`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.bar_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.bar_inv","kind":"theorem","line":363,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/bar-involution.lean#L363-L378","doc":"`bar (x⁻¹) = (bar x)⁻¹` over a field. From `bar(x · x⁻¹) = bar 1 = 1`\nand the multiplicativity of bar. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.barSkewProjection_idempotent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.barSkewProjection_idempotent","kind":"theorem","line":344,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/bar-involution.lean#L344-L347","doc":"**`P_skew` is idempotent**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.barSkewProjection_isBarAntiSymmetric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.barSkewProjection_isBarAntiSymmetric","kind":"theorem","line":329,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/bar-involution.lean#L329-L342","doc":"**`P_skew(x)` is bar-anti-symmetric** for every `x : R`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.barSymmetricProjection_idempotent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.barSymmetricProjection_idempotent","kind":"theorem","line":322,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/bar-involution.lean#L322-L327","doc":"**`P_avg` is idempotent**: applying twice = applying once.\nFollows directly from `barSymmetricProjection_isBarSymmetric`\nand `barSymmetricProjection_of_sym`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.barSymmetricProjection_isBarSymmetric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.barSymmetricProjection_isBarSymmetric","kind":"theorem","line":313,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/bar-involution.lean#L313-L320","doc":"**`P_avg(x)` is bar-symmetric** for every `x : R`. Uses\n`bar_half` (proved above). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.barSkewProjection_pow_odd_of_antisym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.barSkewProjection_pow_odd_of_antisym","kind":"theorem","line":307,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/bar-involution.lean#L307-L311","doc":"$P_{\\mathrm{skew}}(h^{2n+1}) = h^{2n+1}$ on odd powers of bar-anti-sym. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.barSkewProjection_pow_even_of_antisym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.barSkewProjection_pow_even_of_antisym","kind":"theorem","line":301,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/bar-involution.lean#L301-L305","doc":"$P_{\\mathrm{skew}}(h^{2n}) = 0$ on even powers of bar-anti-sym. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.barSymmetricProjection_pow_odd_of_antisym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.barSymmetricProjection_pow_odd_of_antisym","kind":"theorem","line":292,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/bar-involution.lean#L292-L299","doc":"**Odd powers of bar-anti-symmetric: $P_{\\mathrm{avg}}(h^{2n+1}) = 0$**.\nThe bar-symmetric projection kills odd powers — the categorical\ncontent of \"$h, h^3, h^5, \\ldots$ are projected away by\n$P_{\\mathrm{avg}}$\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.barSymmetricProjection_pow_even_of_antisym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.barSymmetricProjection_pow_even_of_antisym","kind":"theorem","line":283,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/bar-involution.lean#L283-L290","doc":"**Even powers of bar-anti-symmetric: $P_{\\mathrm{avg}}(h^{2n}) = h^{2n}$**.\nThe bar-symmetric projection acts as identity on even powers of a\nbar-anti-symmetric kernel — the categorical content of \"$h^2,\nh^4, h^6, \\ldots$ are kept by $P_{\\mathrm{avg}}$\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.barSkewProjection_of_sym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.barSkewProjection_of_sym","kind":"theorem","line":276,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/bar-involution.lean#L276-L281","doc":"`P_skew(x) = 0` when `x` is bar-symmetric. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.barSkewProjection_of_antisym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.barSkewProjection_of_antisym","kind":"theorem","line":268,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/bar-involution.lean#L268-L274","doc":"`P_skew(x) = x` when `x` is bar-anti-symmetric. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.barSymmetricProjection_of_antisym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.barSymmetricProjection_of_antisym","kind":"theorem","line":261,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/bar-involution.lean#L261-L266","doc":"`P_avg(x) = 0` when `x` is bar-anti-symmetric. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.barSymmetricProjection_of_sym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.barSymmetricProjection_of_sym","kind":"theorem","line":253,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/bar-involution.lean#L253-L259","doc":"`P_avg(x) = x` when `x` is bar-symmetric. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.isBarSymmetric_intCast","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.isBarSymmetric_intCast","kind":"theorem","line":244,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/bar-involution.lean#L244-L251","doc":"Every integer scalar is bar-symmetric (pure `CommRing` content). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.bar_invOf_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.bar_invOf_two","kind":"theorem","line":226,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/bar-involution.lean#L226-L241","doc":"`bar(⅟2) = ⅟2`. Foundation for `barSymmetricProjection` idempotency.\nOver a `CommRing`: `bar(⅟2)·2 = bar(⅟2·2) = bar 1 = 1`, and the inverse\nof `2` is unique — no division, and no field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.isBarSymmetric_natCast","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.isBarSymmetric_natCast","kind":"theorem","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/bar-involution.lean#L207-L209","doc":"Every natural-number scalar is bar-symmetric. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.bar_natCast","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.bar_natCast","kind":"theorem","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/bar-involution.lean#L198-L205","doc":"`bar` fixes every natural-number scalar. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.bar_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.bar_two","kind":"theorem","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/bar-involution.lean#L193-L196","doc":"`bar 2 = 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.IsBarAntiSymmetric.pow_two_mul_add_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.IsBarAntiSymmetric.pow_two_mul_add_one","kind":"theorem","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/bar-involution.lean#L174-L180","doc":"**Odd powers of a bar-anti-symmetric element are bar-anti-symmetric.**\nDirect corollary: `h^(2n+1)` is bar-anti-symmetric. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.IsBarAntiSymmetric.pow_two_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.IsBarAntiSymmetric.pow_two_mul","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/bar-involution.lean#L158-L172","doc":"**Even powers of a bar-anti-symmetric element are bar-symmetric.**\nDirect corollary: `h^(2n)` is bar-symmetric for any bar-anti-sym `h`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.IsBarAntiSymmetric.neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.IsBarAntiSymmetric.neg","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/bar-involution.lean#L152-L156","doc":"Negation of bar-anti-symmetric is bar-anti-symmetric. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.IsBarSymmetric.neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.IsBarSymmetric.neg","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/bar-involution.lean#L146-L150","doc":"Negation of bar-symmetric is bar-symmetric. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.bar_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.bar_neg","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/bar-involution.lean#L139-L144","doc":"`bar (-x) = -bar x` — bar commutes with negation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.IsBarAntiSymmetric.of_sym_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.IsBarAntiSymmetric.of_sym_mul","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/bar-involution.lean#L132-L137","doc":"Sym × anti-sym = anti-sym. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.IsBarSymmetric.of_mul_antisym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.IsBarSymmetric.of_mul_antisym","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/bar-involution.lean#L122-L130","doc":"**Anti-sym × anti-sym = bar-symmetric** — the key \"even pair → even\"\nidentity. Concretely produces $h^2$ bar-symmetric from $h$\nbar-anti-symmetric; same identity that makes $\\cosh(h)$ and\n$\\mathrm{Li}_2^q$ bar-symmetric. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.IsBarAntiSymmetric.add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.IsBarAntiSymmetric.add","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/bar-involution.lean#L115-L120","doc":"Sum of bar-anti-symmetric elements is bar-anti-symmetric. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.IsBarSymmetric.mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.IsBarSymmetric.mul","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/bar-involution.lean#L108-L113","doc":"Product of bar-symmetric elements is bar-symmetric. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.IsBarSymmetric.add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.IsBarSymmetric.add","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/bar-involution.lean#L101-L106","doc":"Sum of bar-symmetric elements is bar-symmetric. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.isBarSymmetric_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.isBarSymmetric_one","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/bar-involution.lean#L98-L99","doc":"`1` is bar-symmetric. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.isBarSymmetric_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.isBarSymmetric_zero","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/bar-involution.lean#L95-L96","doc":"`0` is bar-symmetric. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.decompose","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.decompose","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/bar-involution.lean#L74-L78","doc":"Every element decomposes as `x = P_avg(x) + P_skew(x)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.barSkewProjection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.barSkewProjection","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/bar-involution.lean#L70-L72","doc":"`P_skew = (1 - bar)/2`, written with the unit `⅟2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.barSymmetricProjection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.barSymmetricProjection","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/bar-involution.lean#L66-L68","doc":"`P_avg = (1 + bar)/2`, written with the unit `⅟2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.IsBarAntiSymmetric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.IsBarAntiSymmetric","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/bar-involution.lean#L52-L54","doc":"Predicate: `x` is bar-anti-symmetric (bar-odd). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.IsBarSymmetric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.IsBarSymmetric","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/bar-involution.lean#L48-L50","doc":"Predicate: `x` is bar-symmetric (bar-even). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.BarInvolution.bar_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.BarInvolution.bar_zero","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/bar-involution.lean#L46-L46","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.BarInvolution.bar_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.BarInvolution.bar_one","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/bar-involution.lean#L45-L45","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.BarInvolution.bar_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.BarInvolution.bar_mul","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/bar-involution.lean#L44-L44","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.BarInvolution.bar_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.BarInvolution.bar_add","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/bar-involution.lean#L43-L43","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.BarInvolution.bar_involutive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.BarInvolution.bar_involutive","kind":"theorem","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/bar-involution.lean#L42-L42","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.BarInvolution.bar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.BarInvolution.bar","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/bar-involution.lean#L41-L41","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.BarInvolution.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.BarInvolution.mk","kind":"ctor","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/bar-involution.lean#L40-L40","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.BarInvolution","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvolutionDef.BarInvolution","kind":"class","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/bar-involution.lean#L36-L46","doc":"The bar-involution `σ ↦ σ⁻¹` / `q ↦ q⁻¹` on a generic\ncommutative ring (typically the coefficient field\n`ℤ[q^{±1/2}, (q-q⁻¹)⁻¹]` or its archimedean specialisation\n`ℝ`). Records the four ring-involution axioms. ","signatureChunk":0}]}